 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all. The pauses before the remaining
+attempts are 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds, as implemented in [capture.py](../../larder/capture.py). If the fifth attempt
+times out, the exception is raised to the caller. The pauses add up to 20 seconds of waiting on the confirmation
+page, in addition to the time spent calling the gateway.
+
+Previously, the three attempts went out back to back within a second, all during the same gateway slowdown. The
+gateway's Friday peak from 17:00 to 19:00 left 58 confirmed pantry orders uncharged one Friday; a payments volunteer
+captured them manually the next morning. Replaying those timeouts in the sandbox with the current pauses would
+have captured 57 of the 58 pantry orders. The maintainers accepted the extra wait to reduce that manual work;
+switching gateways was ruled out that year because the contract ran through December 2026. This discussion and
+the merged change are recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
